                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_symplectic_manifolds"} Relation to symplectic manifolds
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_spinstructures"} Relation to Spin-structures
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#HodgeStarOperator"} Hodge star operator
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#HodgeStructure"} Hodge structure
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_riemannian_manifolds"}
                    As
                    = succeed "-Riemannian" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ℂ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              %li
                %a{:href => "#kapranov_algebras"}
                  Kapranov
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{\infty}
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Kähler manifold
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            compatibly equipped with
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"}> complex structure
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+structure"}> Riemannian structure
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+structure"}> symplectic structure
                \.
          %p
            If the symplectic structure is not compatibly present, it is just a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+manifold"} Hermitian manifold
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
                %th
                  +
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+structure"} Riemannian structure
                %th
                  +
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+structure"} symplectic structure
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+structure"} Hermitian structure
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+structure"} Kähler structure
          %p
            Where a Riemannian manifold is a real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            equipped with a nondegenerate smooth symmetric 2-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            %strong almost Kähler manifold
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex holomorphic manifold
            equipped with a nondegenerate hermitian 2-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            (the
            = succeed ")." do
              %strong
                Kähler
                = succeed "-form" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
            is replaced with the complex cotangent bundle, and symmetry is replaced with hermitian symmetry. An almost Kähler manifold is a
            %strong Kähler manifold
            if it satisfies an additional integrability condition.
          %p
            The Kähler 2-form can be decomposed as
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo +
                    %mi i
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h = g+i\omega
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3{:id => "LinearKählerStructure"} Linear Kähler structure
          #KaehlerVectorSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+vector+space"}> Kähler vector space
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              %em linear Kähler structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+complex+structure"} linear complex structure
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        J \;\colon\; V \to V
                %p
                  whose
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  with itself is minus the
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi J
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        J \circ J = - id_V
              %li
                %p
                  a skew-symmetric
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mn 2
                        %msup
                          %mi V
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\omega \in \wedge^2 V^\ast
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega(J(-),J(-)) = \omega(-,-)
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(-,-) \coloneqq \omega(-,J(-))
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
                %p
                  a non-degenerate positive-definite
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %p
                  (necessarily symmetric, due to the other properties:
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi w
                          %mo ,
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi w
                          %mo ,
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi v
                          %mo ,
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi v
                          %mo ,
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(w,v) = \omega(w,J(v)) = -\omega(J(v),w) = - \omega(J(J(v)), J(w)) = +\omega(v,J(w)) = g(v,w)
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Boalch09"} Boalch 09, p. 26-27
          %p
            Linear Kähler space structure may conveniently be encoded in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+space"} Hermitian space
            structure:
          #HermitianForm.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+form"} Hermitian form
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+space"} Hermitian space
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\colon V \to V
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+form"} Hermitian form
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a complex-valued real-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi ℂ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        h \;\colon\; V \otimes V \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}
            %p
              such that this is
              = succeed "," do
                %em symmetric sesquilinear
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
                  is complex-linear in the first argument;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi w
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(w,v) = \left(h(v,w) \right)^\ast
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v,w \in V
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\ast
              denotes
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+conjugation"} complex conjugation
            %p
              A Hermitian form is
              %em positive definite
              (often assumed by default) if for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(v,v) \geq 0
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                        %mo ⇔
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                        %mi v
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(v,v) = 0 \phantom{AA} \Leftrightarrow \phantom{AA} v = 0
                  \.
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+space"} complex vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,J)
              equipped with a (positive definite) Hermitian form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              is called a (positive definite)
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+space"} Hermitian space
          #BasicPropertiesOfHermitianForms.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (basic properties of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+forms"} Hermitian forms
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((V,J),h)
              be a positive definite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+space"} Hermitian space
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HermitianForm"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+part"} real part
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+form"} Hermitian form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Re
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g(-,-) \;\coloneqq\; Re(h(-,-))
                %p
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g \;\colon\; V \otimes V \to \mathbb{R}
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+part"} imaginary part
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+form"} Hermitian form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo −
                        %mi Im
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\omega(-,-) \;\coloneqq\; -Im(h(-,-))
                %p
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi V
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\omega \;\colon\; V \wedge V \to \mathbb{R}
                        \\,.
            %p hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo −
                    %mi i
                    %mi ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h = g - i \omega
                    \\,.
            %p The two components are related by
            #eq:RelationBetweennOmegaAndgOnHermitianSpace.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAAA
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega(v,w)
                    \\;=\;
                    g(J(v),w)
                    \\phantom{AAAAA}
                    g(v,w)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\omega(v,J(v))
                    \\,.
            %p Finally
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h(J(-),J(-)) = h(-,-)
            %p
              and so the Riemannian metrics
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              appearing from (and fully determining) Hermitian forms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              via
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo −
                    %mi i
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h = g - i \omega
              are precisely those for which
            #eq:HermitianMetric.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g(J(-),J(-)) = g(-,-)
                    \\,.
            %p
              These are called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+metrics"} Hermitian metrics
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The positive-definiteness of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              is immediate from that of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              follows from the symmetric sesquilinearity of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo ,
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mi Re
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo ,
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Re
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi h
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi v
                              %mo ,
                              %mi w
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo *
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Re
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    g(w,v)
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    Re(h(w,v))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Re\left( h(v,w)^\ast\right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Re(h(v,w))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    g(v,w)
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              is invariant under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              follows from its sesquilinarity
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi i
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo ,
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    h(J(v),J(w))
                    \&amp;=
                    i h(v,J(w))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    i (h(J(w),v))^\ast
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    i (-i) (h(w,v))^\ast
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    h(v,w)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              and this immediately implies the corresponding invariance of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %p
              Analogously it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              is skew symmetric:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo ,
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi Im
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo ,
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi Im
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi h
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi v
                              %mo ,
                              %mi w
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo *
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Im
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\omega(w,v)
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \-Im(h(w,v))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \-Im\left( h(v,w)^\ast\right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Im(h(v,w))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = - \omega(v,w)
                    \\,,
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p and the relation between the two components:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi Im
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Re
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Re
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\omega(v,w)
                    \&amp; =
                    \- Im(h(v,w))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Re(i h(v,w))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Re(h(J(v),w))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    g(J(v),w)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p as well as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Re
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Im
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Im
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Im
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi J
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi Im
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    g(v,w)
                    \&amp; =
                    Re(h(v,w)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Im(i h(v,w))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Im(h(J(v),w))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Im(h(J^2(v),J(w)))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \- Im(h(v,J(w)))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = \omega(v,J(w))
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
          %p As a corollary:
          #RelationBetweenKaehlerVectorSpacesAndHermitianSpaces.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (relation between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+vector+spaces"} Kähler vector spaces
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+spaces"} Hermitian spaces
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+complex+structure"} linear complex structure
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mn 2
                        %msup
                          %mi V
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \wedge^2 V^\ast
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+K%C3%A4hler+structure"} linear Kähler structure
                  (def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KaehlerVectorSpace"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in V \otimes V \to  \mathbb{R}
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+metric"} Hermitian metric
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HermitianMetric"} (2)
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              are related by
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RelationBetweennOmegaAndgOnHermitianSpace"} (1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAAA
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega(v,w)
                    \\;=\;
                    g(J(v),w)
                    \\phantom{AAAAA}
                    g(v,w)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\omega(v,J(w))
                    \\,.
          %h3#khler_manifolds Kähler manifolds
          %p (…)
          %h3#InTermsOfGStructure
            In terms of
            = succeed "-Structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            A Kähler manifold is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrability+of+G-structure"} first-order integrable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+Hermitian+structure"} almost Hermitian structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = U(n) \hookrightarrow GL(2n,\mathbb{R})
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
          %p
            By the fact (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "unitary+group#RelationToOrthogonalSymplecticAndGeneralLinearGroup"} unitary group – relation to orthogonal, symplectic and general linear group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n) \simeq O(2n) \underset{GL(2n,\mathbb{R})}{\times} Sp(2n,\mathbb{R}) \underset{GL(2n,\mathbb{R})}{\times} GL(n,\mathbb{C})
            this means that a Kähler manifold structure is precisely a joint
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            structure,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            structure and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            structure.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Moroianu07"} Moroianu 07, 11.1
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Verbitsky09"} Verbitsky 09
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p The archetypical elementary example is the following:
          #StandardAlmostKaehlerVectorSpaces.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (standard
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+vector+space"} Kähler vector space
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \coloneqq \mathbb{R}^2
              be the 2-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              which is given by the canonical identification
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2 \simeq \mathbb{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_i)
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J = (J^i{}_j)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; -1
                    \\\
                    1 &amp; 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p Moreover let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega = (\omega_{i j}) \coloneqq \left( \array{0 &amp; 1 \\ -1 &amp; 0} \right)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g = (g_{i j}) \coloneqq \left( \array{ 1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 1}  \right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V, J, \omega, g)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+vector+space"} Kähler vector space
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KaehlerVectorSpace"}
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} Kähler manifold
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
              regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              in the standard way and equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+forms"} bilinear forms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J, \omega g
              extended as constant rank-2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensors"} tensors
              over this manifold.
            %p If we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x,y \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^2 \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            %p
              for the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+functions"} coordinate functions
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
              with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi i
                    %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    z \coloneqq x + i y \;\coloneqq\; \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{C}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi i
                    %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\overline{z} \coloneqq x - i y \;\coloneqq\; \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{C}
            %p for the corresponding complex coordinates, then this translates to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega
                    \\in
                    \\Omega^2(\mathbb{R}^2)
            %p
              being the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+2-form"} differential 2-form
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ω
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi d
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi d
                            %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                              %mfrac
                                %mi i
                                %mn 2
                            %mi d
                            %mi z
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi d
                            %mover
                              %mi z
                              %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\omega
                    \&amp; =
                    d x \wedge d y
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\tfrac{i}{2} d z \wedge d \overline{z}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              and with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor"} tensor
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %mi d
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi d
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi d
                    %mi y
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi d
                    %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g = d x \otimes d x + d y \otimes d y
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+form"} Hermitian form
              is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi h
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi g
                            %mo −
                            %mi i
                            %mi ω
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi d
                            %mi z
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi d
                            %mover
                              %mi z
                              %mo ¯
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    h
                    \&amp; =
                    g - i \omega
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    d z \otimes d \overline{z}
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              This is elementary, but, for the record, here is one way to make it fully explicit (we use
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+summation+convention"} Einstein summation convention
              and “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdot
              ” denotes
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+multiplication"} matrix multiplication
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                                %mo ′
                            %msup
                              %mi J
                              %mrow
                                %mi j
                                %mo ′
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 0
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 1
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 0
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 0
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mn 1
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 0
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 0
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 0
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 1
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\omega_{i j'} J^{j'}{}_j
                    \&amp; =
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; 1
                    \\\
                    \-1 &amp; 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\cdot
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; -1
                    \\\
                    1 &amp; 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
