          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fubini-Study+metric"}> Fubini-Study metric
                )
            %p
              There is a unique (up to a scalar) hermitian metric on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
              (which may be normalized), the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fubini-Study+metric"} Fubini-Study metric
            %p
              All analytic subvarieties of a complex projective space are in fact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+variety"} algebraic subvarieties
              and they inherit the Kähler structure from the projective space.
            %p
              Examples include
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+tori"} complex tori
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^n/L
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is a lattice in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surfaces"} K3-surfaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+manifolds"} Calabi-Yau manifolds
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_almost_complex_manifold Relation to (almost) complex manifold
          %blockquote
            %p
              The following based on
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/73330/381"} this MO comment
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spiro+Karigiannis"} Spiro Karigiannis
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, J)
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+complex+manifold"} almost complex manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            of type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is of type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,1)
            precisely if it satisfies
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega(J v,J w) = \omega(v,w)
          %p
            for all smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+fields"} vector fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v,w
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is a
            %em real
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ω
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo =
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline \omega = \omega
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g(v,w) = \omega(v, J w),
          %p
            defines a smooth symmetric rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,0)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+field"} tensor field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            precisely if it is fiberwise a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+definite+bilinear+form"} positive definite bilinear form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(-,-) = \omega(-,J -)
            is hence a Riemannian metric, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega(-,-)
            is called positive definite, too.
          %p
            The triple of data
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J, \omega, g)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+complex+structure"} almost complex structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is a real positive
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is the associated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            this way define an
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+Hermitian+manifold"} almost Hermitian manifold
          %p
            Now the condition for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be a Kähler is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is integrable) and that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\omega = 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+connection"} Levi-Civita connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mi ω
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla \omega = 0
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla J = 0
          %p
            Hence given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em closed
            real
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            = succeed "-form." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,1)
          %h3#relation_to_symplectic_manifolds Relation to symplectic manifolds
          %p
            Lifting a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            structure to a Kähler manifold structure is also called choosing a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+polarization"} Kähler polarization
          %h3#relation_to_spinstructures Relation to Spin-structures
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              A spin structure on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+manifold"} Hermitian manifold
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifold"}> Kähler manifold
              )
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              exists precisely if, equivalently
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  there is a choice of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+root"} square root
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msqrt
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{\Omega^{n,0}}
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+line+bundle"} canonical line bundle
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{n,0}
                  (a “
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+characteristic"}> Theta characteristic
                  ”);
              %li
                %p
                  there is a trivialization of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1(T X)
                  of the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
          %p In this case one has:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mo •
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %msqrt
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 0
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S_X \simeq \Omega^{0,\bullet}_X \otimes \sqrt{\Omega^{n,0}}_X
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundle"} spinor bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_X
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+complex"} Dolbeault complex
              with the corresponding
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+characteristic"} Theta characteristic
            %p
              Moreover, the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault-Dirac+operator"} Dolbeault-Dirac operator
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mo ∂
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\partial} + \overline{\partial}^\ast
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Hitchin74"}> Hitchin 74
            ). A textbook account is for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Friedrich74"}> Friedrich 74, around p. 79 and p. 82
            ).
