          %h2#references References
          %p
            Kähler manifolds were first introduced and studied by P. A. Shirokov (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1070/RM1995v050n02ABEH002098"} a historical article
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Voisin02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claire+Voisin"}> Claire Voisin
                , section 3 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+theory+and+Complex+algebraic+geometry"} Hodge theory and Complex algebraic geometry
                    I,II
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 76, 77
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ana+Cannas+da+Silva"}> Ana Cannas da Silva
                , §16 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Symplectic Geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1764
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-45330-7"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-45330-7
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li#Moroianu07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Moroianu"}> Andrei Moroianu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Kähler Geometry
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0402223"} arXiv:math/0402223
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511618666"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511618666
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://moroianu.perso.math.cnrs.fr/tex/kg.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Boalch09
              %p
                Philip Boalch,
                %em Noncompact complex symplectic and hyperkähler manifolds
                (2009) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~philip.boalch/cours09/hk.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Boalch-NoncompactSymplectic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrability+of+G-structure"} first-order integrable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Moroianu07"} Moroianu 07, 11.1
            %li#Verbitsky09
              %p
                Misha Verbitsky,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kähler manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://verbit.ru/MATH/TALKS/Unicamp-kahler-1.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structures"} spin structures
            in Kähler manifolds is for instance in
          %ul
            %li#Friedrich97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Friedrich"}> Thomas Friedrich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dirac operators in Riemannian geometry
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+theory"} Hodge theory
            on Kähler manifolds is in
          %ul
            %li#BiquerdHoering08
              O. Biquard, A. Höring,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Kähler geometry and Hodge theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~hoering/hodge/hodge.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On Kapranov’s
            = succeed "-structure:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{\infty}
          %ul
            %li#Kapranov99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"}> Mikhail Kapranov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Rozansky-Witten invariants via Atiyah classes
              %strong 115
              1 (1999) 71-113 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2000h:57056"}> MR2000h:57056
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1023/A:1000664527238"} doi:10.1023/A:1000664527238
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9704009"} arXiv:alg-geom/9704009
          %p
            For further developing of this concept in view of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fedosov+deformation+quantization"} Fedosov deformation quantization
          %ul
            %li#KwokwaiNaichungQin2020
              Kwokwai Chan, Naichung Conan Leung, Qin Li,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Kapranov’s L∞ structures, Fedosov’s star products, and one-loop exact BV quantizations on Kähler manifolds
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.07057"} abs/2008.07057
          %p On quantization of Kähler manifolds:
          %ul
            %li#KwokwaiNaichungQin2020quant
              Kwokwai Chan, Naichung Conan Leung, Qin Li,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantization of Kähler manifolds
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.03690"} abs/2009.03690
          %p
            Discussion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+orbifolds"} Kähler orbifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Thalia D. Jeffres,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Singular Set of Some Kähler Orbifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2155355"} jstor:2155355
            %li
              %p
                Akira Fujiki,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On primitively symplectic compact Kähler V-manifolds
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenji+Ueno"} Kenji Ueno
                (ed.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classification of Algebraic and Analytic Manifolds: Katata Symposium Proceedings 1982
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Joyce"}> Dominic Joyce
                , Section 6.5.1 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Compact Manifolds with Special Holonomy
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/compact-manifolds-with-special-holonomy-9780198506010?cc=de&lang=en&"} ISBN:9780198506010
            %li
              %p
                Miguel Abreu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kähler Metrics on Toric Orbifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1090348285"} euclid:jdg/1090348285
            %li
              %p
                Giovanni Bazzoni, Indranil Biswas, Marisa Fernández, Vicente Muñoz, Aleksy Tralle,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopic properties of Kähler orbifolds
                %em Special Metrics and Group Actions in Geometry
                Springer INdAM Series, vol 23. Springer (2017) (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.03024"}> arXiv:1605.03024
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-67519-0_2"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-67519-0_2
